{"title":"2025 Spring Tournament of Towns Senior A-Level Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_Spring_Tournament_of_Towns_Senior_A-Level_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Does there exist a positive number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/3767f0665ea4d5f0e9c58452fc5782b42a8a65a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/e/6fedd63782e1046d770379f5fdf93f0b8cdbad81.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\{x\\} &gt; \\{x^2\\} &gt; \\{x^3\\} &gt; ...&gt; \\{x^{100}\\}?\\]\" width=\"269\" height=\"20\" />(Here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df2919191b1220773d9b0142dec5c3528fd4c42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> is the fractional part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, that is, the difference between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and the maximal integer not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_Spring_Tournament_of_Towns_Senior_A-Level_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer is YES.\n</p><p><br />\nAssume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/3660f38987c844cf9574682dd0bd2d38c6f23018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=n+0.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/4/5040abd331d0e8f732c22df007be99377aaac42d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=n^2+n+0.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26c7528b3e65d81f05115bfd333755a3d761013d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3=n^3+1.5n^2+0.75n+0.125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWe can notice that, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> contains a very large power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as a factor, all the terms before the final term will be an integer, which does not affect the fractional part at all.\n</p><p>For example, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/0883b5f788a7c5fda85015343021eca5fb628382.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^3+1.5n^2+0.75n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" /> will be an integer.\n</p><p><br />\nAs a result, we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9ed34e0825a1f04589450292fa0d44263b7147c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2^{100}+0.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/4/8844c5d2305061939c690cf2016c8ca8297cad25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^j=(2^{100}+0.5)^j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28c37c8df6264a6aef623e06f8d31789e3b8924d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=(2^{100})^j+j{(2^{100})}^{j-1}\\times{0.5}+\\tbinom{j}{2}{(2^{100})}^{j-2}\\times{0.5^2}+\\tbinom{j}{3}{(2^{100})}^{j-3}\\times{0.5^3}+......+\\tbinom{j}{j-1}2^{100}\\times{0.5^{j-1}}+0.5^j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"814\" height=\"29\" />\n</p><p><br />\nAs we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/0107d041c83ec9846603fa136199a0c9159995e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j\\leq{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />, all the terms before the final term are integers, which do not affect the fractional part.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/645dfd88a2f3dbfdc270ab22831908631850def1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x^j\\}=0.5^j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"22\" />, which is a strictly decreasing sequence.\n</p><p><br />\nThis completes the proof.\n</p><p><br />\n~G2JFForever\n</p><p>A small addition:\nIF WE TAKE ANY NUMBER (NOT AN INTEGER) AND SQUARE TO CUBE IT, THE DECIMAL PART ALWAYS DECREASES, AS ANY NUMBER = (X+Y), Y IS DECIMAL,\n(X+Y) TO THE N WOULD ALWAYS PRESENT A SMALLER EXPRESSION BEHIND THE SECIMAL POINT BY BINOMIAL EXPANSION.\n</p><p>THANK YOU\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018033047\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.019 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 74/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3595/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36625:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018033047 and revision id 289916. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}